<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Atarneus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Atarneus was an ancient Greek town on the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysia">Mysia</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a>, opposite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lesbos">Lesbos</a>. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> gave its district to Chios in return for surrendering the Lydian rebel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pactyes">Pactyes</a>. In the fourth century BCE it was ruled by Hermias, a friend of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plato">Plato</a>'s Academy, at whose court <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristotle">Aristotle</a> lived for a time.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/atarneus.jpg" alt="Atarneus" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mr. Erkmen Senan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atarna(Atarneus)_Dikili_Turkey.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
